    {
      "id": "b7hjxo1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to High Courts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 214 provides that there shall be a High Court for each State in India.",
        "High Court judges are appointed by the President after consultation with the Chief Justice of India and the State Governor.",
        "A High Court judge holds office until attaining the age of 62 years.",
        "High Courts have the power to issue writs under Article 226 for fundamental rights and other legal rights.",
        "Parliament has the power to establish a common High Court for two or more states or Union Territories under Article 231."
      ],
      "id": "gggrs5u"
    },
